+	 * controller once it is done with it.  Claiming a slot that is still
+	 * held does nothing whatever, so one request that never finished would
+	 * otherwise take down every request after it.  Take the slot back
+	 * first.  The register that releases it is written twice, with the
+	 * mask and with its complement, because only one slot is ever in use
+	 * here and that way it does not matter which way round the register
+	 * reads.
